text:
{
  "factual_errors": [
    "The summary states the pending winding-up petition was filed on 19 Feb 2024, but the record shows it was filed on 19 Feb 2024 (CASE-2024-5611) is actually correct, however the summary lists it as 'filed 19 Feb 2024' while the record for CASE-2024-5611 is 2024-02-19, which matches; however, the summary lists the pending tenancy dispute filed 29 Jan 2025 as RM559.5k, which matches CASE-2025-5224, but the summary lists the pending tenancy dispute filed 25 Sep 2025 as RM122.1k, which matches CASE-2025-6165; the error is that the summary describes the company as a 'Boutique hotel operator in Penang' while the record lists the state as 'Selangor' and nature of business as 'Boutique hotel in Penang', which is a contradiction in location/state registration vs business location, but more critically, the summary states 'two appointed in 2025' for directors, but the record shows Director 1 appointed 2025-01-29 and no other director appointed in 2025 (Director 3 was 2023, Director 4 2015, Director 5 2021, Director 2 2014), so only one director was appointed in 2025."
  ],
  "missed_risks": [
    "The summary omits the pending debt recovery case (CASE-2025-8120) which was withdrawn, but more importantly, it omits the fact that the company has a history of multiple winding-up petitions (2023, 2024, 2025) indicating severe liquidity or solvency issues, although the 2025 one was withdrawn, the pattern is a major risk not fully contextualized as a recurring issue."
  ],
  "misleading": [
    "The summary labels the risk as 'Elevated' but the presence of a pending winding-up petition (even if small) combined with high leverage (2.50x) and a history of similar petitions suggests a 'High' or 'Critical' risk level for a supplier vetting context, as it threatens the company's continued existence."
  ],
  "accuracy": 3,
  "risk_coverage": 3,
  "usefulness": 4,
  "concision": 5
}

